note left of confirmed
  202610170001: a new disruption flag returns Preparation/Confirmed
  to Planning, clears confirmed_by/at, writes history and notifies
  the Coordinator and Organiser. Other event details remain.
  202610210002 (SG2-83): cancelling a venue booking, or asking to
  change one, does the same through
  return_event_to_planning_for_venue.
  202610170002: confirmation refuses affected bookings AND
  persisted venue/equipment/registration rechecks.
  202610220001 (SG2-94): confirmation also needs the latest safety
  decision to be Approve; leaving Preparation/Confirmed withdraws it.
end note

note right of cancelled
  SG2-67 (202610220002): the creating Organiser asks
  (POST /:id/cancellation-request, rpc request_event_cancellation);
  only the assigned Coordinator carries it out (cancel_event).
  cancel_event releases bookings, holds and pending requests and
  notifies attendees and the Organiser; SG2-56 (202610210001)
  releases equipment when status becomes cancelled.
  keep_cancelled_events_cancelled refuses any later status change.
  Not cancellable: draft (deleted instead), rejected, completed,
  and unassigned (no coordinator yet to carry it out).
end note

note as changes
  Event change requests (SG2-64/65/66): POST /:id/change-requests raises
  one on any status except draft, cancelled, rejected or completed;
  it changes no status. Accepting applies the change on approved,
  planning, awaiting_safety_check, preparation and confirmed events
  (apply_accepted_event_change: a change that leaves a recheck
  outstanding returns an Approved, Awaiting Safety Check, Preparation
  or Confirmed event to Planning, and a significant change also
  returns Preparation/Confirmed and withdraws the safety approval).
  On needs_clarification the change is written to the request and
  next = 'review' moves it to under_review ('resubmit' keeps it).
  Refusing (POST .../refuse) leaves the status as it is.
end note

note as enforcement
  STATUS_TRANSITIONS and canTransition() were removed from
  server/src/events/fields.ts by PR #120 (SG2-22, commit ca54162);
  no transition table exists now; each handler or RPC checks its own
  accepted statuses. This diagram is drawn
  from the writers. updatePlanning.ts refuses only
  cancelled/completed/rejected and refuses Preparation/Confirmed edits
  to locked fields (change request needed), but sets status = 'planning'
  on any edit with arrangement impact (a date shift or attendance
  increase against a live venue/equipment arrangement) and on the
  first edit of an approved event. Any status the handler accepts,
  incl. submitted / under_review / needs_clarification / safety_rejected,
  would therefore return to planning on such an edit; only the
  awaiting_safety_check and approved edges are drawn.
  The database blocks only two moves: safety_approval_gate (into
  Preparation) and keep_cancelled_events_cancelled (out of cancelled).
end note

